tner has just explained what happened, so do NOT ask what happened and do NOT ask any question of your own. In ONE short natural sentence state the MDND deduction on their ticket from the call context — amount, date and order-ID last four digits — for example \'आपके ticket पर MDND का deduction 500 रुपये का है, जो 25 अगस्त को हुआ था, और ऑर्डर का आखिरी चार अंक 9456 हैं।\'. Never mention any other deduction. The flow\'s next step follows in the same reply; keep it as authored. If the context has no ticket details, say nothing about the ticket.\", \"responseDirective\": \"Open the enquiry the way a Zepto support agent reads a ticket. From the call context, briefly state ONLY the MDND deduction on the partner\'s ticket: its amount, date and order-ID last four digits — for example \'आपके ticket पर MDND का deduction 500 रुपये का है, जो 25 अगस्त को हुआ था, और ऑर्डर का आखिरी चार अंक 9456 हैं।\'. Never mention any other deduction or fee, and never ask the partner to choose between concerns. Then ask what happened — \'बताइए — क्या हुआ था?\'. Natural Hinglish, at most two short sentences plus the question. If the context has no ticket or deduction details, simply ask them to describe what happened; the structured flow will ask only the still-missing amount, date or order last-four afterward. Use `partner_name` at most once and never use an end-customer name as the caller\'s name. Never invent any value.\", \"responseMustInclude\": [\"क्या हुआ था\"], \"unmatchedReplyByLanguage\": {\"en\": \"Sorry, I couldn\'t understand that. What happened with this delivery?\"}, \"acceptUnderstoodNarrative\": true, \"responseMustIncludeByLanguage\": {\"en\": [\"what happened\"]}}}, {\"x\": 560, \"y\": 40, \"id\": \"n_ask_amount\", \"kind\": \"ask\", \"label\": \"Missing deduction amount\", \"config\": {\"entity\": {\"dataType\": \"text\", \"regexPattern\": \"[0-9]{2,6}(?=\\\\s*(?:rupees?|rs\\\\b|रुपये|रुपए|रूपये|रुपैये))|(?<=₹)\\\\s?[0-9]{2,6}\"}, \"question\": \"MDND का deduction amount कितना 